s 72.5 hours → pending too long → fail, N=72.\n\nWith the option, pending proof younger than H hours → exit 0.\n\nHow to structure: in cmd_check_anchors, for ots anchors with existed_by == \"pending\" (i.e., check_ots returned None), we need the sigstore attestation time. We could call check_sigstore for that seq too (it verifies writer ranges). Actually check_sigstore verifies the anchor file for that seq and returns integratedTime t.\n\nLet me view the whole file portions to understand: cmd_check_anchors loop, check_sigstore signature, load_chain, etc.\n\nLet me read record.py fully around relevant parts.", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "grep -n \"def \\|integratedTime\\|anchored_at\\|attest\" /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/record.py", "is_input": false, "timeout": null, "reset": false, "kind": "TerminalAction"}, "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "call_7ead0deb0fef4196bbdbfdfb", "tool_call": {"id": "call_7ead0deb0fef4196bbdbfdfb", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "terminal", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"def \\\\|integratedTime\\\\|anchored_at\\\\|attest\\\" /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/record.py\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "gen-1794381560-4ZYjFIAjCMO4mT9Kah8S", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "terminal: {\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"def \\\\|integratedTime\\\\|anchored_at\\\\|attest\\\" /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/record.py\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
