{"id": "67c91086-e520-44c6-b5d8-d6be9ee0cd4f", "timestamp": "2026-11-11T07:21:52.348030", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "call_ff5377a6bcc74eed8c9fa4e2", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Files /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/record.py and /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/record/record.py differ\nFiles /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/test_record.py and /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/record/test_record.py differ\n# Task: `check-anchors` misses a deleted OpenTimestamps proof\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Bug report from an outside verifier:** in a ledger whose entries are covered by Sigstore range attestations, they deleted the OpenTimestamps proof file of a range head (for example `anchors/000002.ots`, where `anchors/000002.sigstore.json` attests the range ending at entry 2). Afterwards `python3 record/record.py check-anchors` still exited 0, so the missing proof went unreported.\n\n**Required behaviour:**\n- `check-anchors` must exit 1 when the `.ots` proof for any attested range head is missing.\n- It must print a message to stderr containing `NNNNNN.ots is missing` (for example `000002.ots is missing`).\n- With the proof present, the existing behaviour must not change.\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`.\n# Task: an orphaned attestation must publish the entries it hid\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Background:** the ledger writer attests ranges of entries with a predicate `{\"from_seq\", \"to_seq\", \"prev_sha256\", \"head_sha256\"}`. If a run attests a range and then fails, an \"orphan\" record explains that attestation. A reviewer found that an orphan explained only by its statement could hide an attested entry, such as a failing verdict.\n\n**Required:** add a function to `record/record.py`:\n\n    _orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None\n\n- `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes (as produced by `R.canonical(entry)`).\n- Return `None` when the decoded entries are exactly the attested range: there are `to_seq - from_seq + 1` of them, the first chains from `pred[\"prev_sha256\"]` (its `prev` field), each next one chains from the previous one's sha256, and the sha256 of the last one's canonical bytes equals `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`.\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\n  - one containing the word `range` when the count is wrong;\n  - one containing `chain` when an entry's `prev` doesn't link;\n  - one containing `head` when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`.\n- Wire it into wherever orphans are checked, so an orphan without valid hidden entries is reported.\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`."}], "is_error": false, "command": "diff -q /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/record.py /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/record/record.py; diff -q /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/ws/record/test_record.py /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/record/test_record.py; cat /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T1.md /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T2.md", "exit_code": 0, "timeout": false, "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "runner", "hostname": "runnervm7aw5e", "working_dir": "/home/runner/work/exagium/exagium", "py_interpreter_path": "/usr/bin/python", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "full_output_save_dir": "/home/runner/.openhands/conversations/60ec433828ef42e09d10fc2fd5057a2f/observations", "kind": "TerminalObservation"}, "action_id": "536739de-efb6-4797-b8